{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\coprod_{j \\in J} \\mathcal{X}_j \\to \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0002": "$x_i : U_i \\to \\coprod_{j \\in J} \\mathcal{X}_j$", "MATH_0003": "$U_i = \\coprod U_{i, j}$", "MATH_0004": "$U_{i, j} \\to \\mathcal{X}_j$", "MATH_0005": "$\\{U_{i, j} \\to U\\}$", "MATH_0006": "$U_{i, j} \\to \\mathcal{X}_j$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-surjective-flat-locally-finite-presentation}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:f697e4951ee4e3b8ca5c00c9ba6a1510d49c128d3f5b6ae7b4ee4b3e42b211f3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:10ae13c1760710496469f331e5389036873a43f26490fdbdecc664e5dd67bbe4", "source_text": "Apply\nLemma <REF_0001>\nto the morphism <MATH_0001>.\n(There is a slight set theoretic issue here -- due to our setup of\nthings -- which we ignore.) To finish, note that a morphism\n<MATH_0002> is given by a\ndisjoint union decomposition <MATH_0003> and morphisms\n<MATH_0004>. Then the fppf covering <MATH_0005>\nand the morphisms <MATH_0006> do the job.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:37a7f502437ec7640a4552d2c912735352ca9a1dca2732995ebe37e4b4121848", "unit_id": "tag:07AN:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$|f| : |\\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-fppf-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:04d1a44efaefd1e6a137ea64d186129c2e7b88c50e201b8feb5283842072bb53", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:51dae059180b1c806378a37f23c7ec1302cbbd760fa994468a5ce19837ada533", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be flat and locally of finite\npresentation. Then <MATH_0002> is open.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:bac4b88cf059087957a3905a7e4b8be4657687e768d860f37bab59984928ac47", "unit_id": "tag:06R7:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$V$", "MATH_0002": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$U$", "MATH_0004": "$U \\to V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0006": "$U \\to V$", "MATH_0007": "$|\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0008": "$|V| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}|$", "MATH_0009": "$|U| \\to |\\mathcal{X}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{morphisms-lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5d7bb2e326b084c7e6e2f533f0855a0d43ff58c937713fcc6e034722f984e946", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:62cccb326322687bdaa5d20d54b0dca100e5586030f169babee3c23d206a8cac", "source_text": "Choose a scheme <MATH_0001> and a smooth surjective morphism <MATH_0002>.\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0003> and a smooth surjective morphism\n<MATH_0004>. By assumption the morphism\nof schemes <MATH_0005> is flat and locally of finite presentation.\nHence <MATH_0006> is open by\nMorphisms, Lemma <REF_0001>.\nBy construction of the topology on <MATH_0007> the map\n<MATH_0008> is open.\nThe map <MATH_0009> is surjective.\nThe result follows from these facts by elementary topology.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:9ecf6ae81a8f2952b1732affc9d4f23cbe47dbfb04029dfa03f27265f04e1a64", "unit_id": "tag:06R7:proof"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-descent-quasi-compact}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:335bd39478024aec251dd74d76932b87aaad30c31003a486ec4656524f42cd0c", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ea7ef42f2d39e684f35a863604445ea0e9e551434d1972d1ed4cd72356823344", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks.\nLet <MATH_0002> be a surjective, flat, locally finitely\npresented morphism of algebraic stacks. If the base change\n<MATH_0003>\nis quasi-compact, then <MATH_0004> is quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1316263c1a57eed0c4fd481bdb73a8d89cb39971909f1c4c6351e06c3bf77fda", "unit_id": "tag:0DQK:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06Q1", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Y}' \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Y}' \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{Z}' = \\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0005": "$|\\mathcal{Z}'| \\to |\\mathcal{Y}'|$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{W} \\subset \\mathcal{Z}'$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{Y}'$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0009": "$$\n\\mathcal{W} \\times_\\mathcal{Z} \\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} =\n\\mathcal{W} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}\n$$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{W} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to\n\\mathcal{Y}' \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-fppf-open}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:018d775a709f9c658e15d6cb8335b657ed8d2e3c375df358a725da1c50da6cfe", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:ab567c1b89f64ed30e2ce7962fa139932f68266e61257e982469697edaaf7a8e", "source_text": "We have to show that given <MATH_0001>\nwith <MATH_0002> quasi-compact, we have\n<MATH_0003> is quasi-compact.\nDenote <MATH_0004>.\nThen <MATH_0005> is open, see\nLemma <REF_0001>. Hence we can find a quasi-compact\nopen substack <MATH_0006> mapping onto\n<MATH_0007>. Because\n<MATH_0008>\nis quasi-compact, we know that\n<MATH_0009>\nis quasi-compact. And the map\n<MATH_0010>\nis surjective, hence we win. Some details omitted.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c4926e32afbae0fec785d22bd6e34ad42581a99ffdfe80df1107435c070dd499", "unit_id": "tag:0DQK:proof"}
